Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:31:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 474/488] [DS4.1] Sampler: one-token counts in the counts
 kernel; top-k and top-p by the row gather

The sampler filled a tensor of ones (seq_lens.new_ones) for the counts kernel
to read every step. The counts kernel's one variant takes 1 as the count and
only writes the counts; get_num_sampled_and_rejected(None, ...) launches it,
and the input batch's declarations include it.

get_top_k_top_p gathered each logits row's top-k and top-p with torch
indexing. It uses the runner's TileLang row gather (gather_rows, a negative
index wrapping as torch's), declared for int32 and int64 indices by
SamplingStates.register_warmups, which the sampler's declarations call.

benchmark_token_counts.py --one times the one-token counts against the fill
and the counts kernel.
